# chorus golden vector: handshake response, protocol v2 message type 0x21.
#
# Committed, and never written by a test. Any implementation of chorus protocol v2 must
# produce these exact bytes from the canonical input in handshake_response.fields, and recover
# exactly those fields from them (docs/protocol.md, "Version 2").
#
# Format: whitespace separated hex bytes, '#' starts a comment.
# Test-only keys (the four X25519 secrets in the .fields file) are public: never use them
# for a real device. The Noise prologue is the 7 bytes of handshake_init before the Noise
# message: 43 48 52 53 00 02 01. Noise_XX_25519_ChaChaPoly_SHA256 (noiseprotocol.org, rev 34).

# frame header: type 0x21, payload length 115 (0x0073), big-endian
21 00 73

# noise, Noise message 2 (<- e, ee, s, es): the server's ephemeral public key
23 B7 BB 8C 91 AE 00 87 11 FB 12 84 67 80 BC DF
1E 06 5F 82 1B DF EC 49 F5 7E 7C 7D CD 4C 48 23

# the server's static public key, encrypted (32 bytes and a 16-byte tag)
27 03 2A 4B FA 62 1B 5F 92 08 C6 91 F1 CC 45 B8
E0 86 61 EC 17 E5 24 42 14 05 4E 80 BF 6B 3A E4
52 1D 95 5C 82 AA 35 30 F7 36 B5 DB 29 00 CD E9

# the payload, encrypted: the server id (length byte, then "chorus-server-test") and a 16-byte tag
28 98 E9 F7 DB 9B 69 A8 BB E2 27 D5 6D 5D 57 18
D7 2A F1 60 BB 6D 0F 26 C1 01 AC 54 D5 B0 8C 29
BE E0 71
